pageType: content
background: { type: solid, color: "$paper" }
notes: |
  Slide 9: Astrophysical Population Synthesis: Masses, Spins, and Origins.
  - Explores the underlying astrophysical demographics of the binary black hole population inferred from hierarchical Bayesian modeling.
  - Details the primary mass spectrum: a broken power-law with a pronounced Gaussian peak at ~35 M_sun, reflecting pulsational pair-instability supernova (PPISN) mass pile-up.
  - Analyzes the effective inspiral spin parameter chi_eff: the observed distribution is peaked narrowly near 0.06 with a small positive skew and minimal negative spin fraction, indicating low intrinsic stellar spins prior to merger.
  - Contrasts two competing formation channels: isolated binary evolution in galactic fields (common envelope, aligned spins, q ~ 1) vs dynamical assembly in dense globular clusters or AGN migration traps (isotropic spin orientations, hierarchical mergers, eccentricities).
elements:
  # Left Rail
  - elementId: rail-bg
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [14, 24, 142, 484]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  - elementId: rail-thumb-1
    elementType: image
    bounds: [18, 30, 134, 84]
    src: "assets/thumb_detectors.png"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: rail-thumb-2
    elementType: image
    bounds: [18, 122, 134, 84]
    src: "assets/thumb_timeline.png"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: rail-thumb-3
    elementType: image
    bounds: [18, 214, 134, 84]
    src: "assets/thumb_catalog.png"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: rail-thumb-4
    elementType: image
    bounds: [18, 306, 134, 84]
    src: "assets/thumb_mass.png"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: rail-divider
    elementType: line
    bounds: [168, 24, 1, 484]
    points: "0,0 0,484"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  # Header
  - elementId: slide-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [185, 24, 475, 34]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      text: "Demographics Reveal Two Competing Merger Pathways"

  - elementId: slide-category
    elementType: text
    bounds: [660, 27, 260, 18]
    content:
      style: "$category"
      align: [right, middle]
      text: "08 · POPULATION SYNTHESIS"

  - elementId: header-rule
    elementType: line
    bounds: [185, 58, 735, 1]
    points: "0,0 735,0"
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  # Center Area: Population Matplotlib Chart
  - elementId: chart-pop
    elementType: image
    bounds: [185, 70, 420, 210]
    src: "assets/population_mass_spin.png"
    fit: { mode: contain }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  # Two Channels Structural Diagram
  - elementId: channel-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [185, 290, 420, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 9.5
      bold: true
      color: "$ink"
      text: "Two Competing Astrophysical Binary Formation Pathways:"

  # Channel A Box: Isolated Field
  - elementId: chan-a-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [185, 310, 205, 130]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$primary" }

  - elementId: chan-a-txt
    elementType: text
    bounds: [192, 316, 191, 118]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      lineHeight: 1.3
      color: "$ink"
      text: |
        <b>Channel A: Isolated Field Binaries</b><br/>
        • Massive stellar binary undergoes common-envelope phase.<br/>
        • Tidal torques align stellar spins parallel to orbit (\( \chi_{\text{eff}} > 0 \)).<br/>
        • Produces mass ratios near unity (\( q \ge 0.7 \)) and low eccentricity.

  # Channel B Box: Dynamical Clusters
  - elementId: chan-b-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [400, 310, 205, 130]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$teal" }

  - elementId: chan-b-txt
    elementType: text
    bounds: [407, 316, 191, 118]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      lineHeight: 1.3
      color: "$ink"
      text: |
        <b>Channel B: Dynamical Cluster Assembly</b><br/>
        • Three-body encounters in globular clusters & AGN migration traps.<br/>
        • Random isotropic spin orientations; negative \( \chi_{\text{eff}} \) allowed.<br/>
        • Remnant black holes merge repeatedly into hierarchical giants.

  # Right Sidebar
  - elementId: side-1-bg
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [625, 75, 295, 110]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  - elementId: side-1-icon
    elementType: icon
    iconName: "fas:mountain"
    bounds: [637, 85, 15, 15]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$primary" }

  - elementId: side-1-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [658, 85, 250, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$muted"
      text: "PPISN MASS PILE-UP"

  - elementId: side-1-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [637, 103, 271, 26]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$highlightBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: side-1-formula
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 107, 261, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$ink"
      text: |
        \( p(m_1) \sim (1-\lambda_g)\, m^{-\alpha} + \lambda_g\, \mathrm{G}(m_1|\mu,\sigma) \)

  - elementId: side-1-desc
    elementType: text
    bounds: [637, 134, 271, 44]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 9
      text: "The distinct Gaussian peak near 34 M☉ reflects pulsational pair-instability supernova shedding, where stars shed outer layers before collapsing."

  - elementId: side-2-bg
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [625, 195, 295, 118]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  - elementId: side-2-icon
    elementType: icon
    iconName: "fas:arrows-split-up-and-left"
    bounds: [637, 205, 15, 15]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$teal" }

  - elementId: side-2-head
    elementType: text
    bounds: [658, 205, 250, 16]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$muted"
      text: "EFFECTIVE INSPIRAL SPIN"

  - elementId: side-2-box
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [637, 223, 271, 26]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$highlightBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$borderHair" }

  - elementId: side-2-formula
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 227, 261, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      bold: true
      color: "$teal"
      text: |
        \( \chi_{\text{eff}} = (m_1 \chi_1 + m_2 \chi_2)/(m_1 + m_2) \approx 0.06 \)

  - elementId: side-2-desc
    elementType: text
    bounds: [637, 254, 271, 52]
    content:
      style: "$body"
      fontSize: 9
      text: "The narrow spin distribution centered near zero confirms that stellar-mass black holes are born with small core spins, disproving extreme Kerr natal spin hypotheses."

  - elementId: side-3-bg
    elementType: shape
    shapeName: rect
    bounds: [625, 323, 295, 108]
    fill: { type: solid, color: "$cardBg" }
    border: { style: solid, width: 1, color: "$border" }

  - elementId: side-3-icon
